  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreCare 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'While volunteering on an advisory board, you review an early research
    plan and notice that it focuses mainly on tumor response. You suggest adding
    more quality-of-life measures when choosing which treatments to move forward.


    <b>Why
    is caregiver feedback like this important when researchers are planning preclinical
    studies?</b>'
  explanation: Caregivers help researchers keep patient comfort and quality of life
    in focus, even before testing begins in humans. Their perspective ensures early-stage
    decisions are guided by real-world priorities, not just lab data. By sharing
    what life is really like for patients, caregivers help scientists design treatments
    that are not only effective in the lab but also practical, tolerable, and meaningful
    for the patients who will ultimately use them.
  correctAnswer: It helps researchers understand how treatments may affect daily
    life, guiding them toward options that balance effectiveness with quality of
    life.
  incorrectAnswer1: It ensures that all treatments studied will have no side effects
    for patients.
  incorrectAnswer2: 'It replaces the need for scientists to monitor side effects
    during laboratory testing. '
  incorrectAnswer3: It helps caregivers decide which treatments should be tested
    further in the lab and which treatments should move forward into clinical trials.
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: PreClinical
